OFFICE OF THE KAZEKAGE -- SUCCESSION FILE: DEATH OF THE FOURTH KAZEKAGE
Sensitive. Cross-referenced with classified Mission Reports.

The Fourth Kazekage, father of the Sand Siblings, led Sunagakure during the
years of the alliance with Otogakure and the joint operation against
Konohagakure. He it was who sealed the One-Tail into his youngest son, Gaara.

Circumstances of death: The Fourth was killed prior to the Konoha operation.
For a time his death was concealed, and his place at the head of the invasion
was taken by an impostor -- the rogue Orochimaru, leader of the Sound, who had
murdered him and assumed his form to lure Sunagakure into the trap. The village
was thus deceived into marching on its former ally.

Consequence: Upon discovery of the deception, Sunagakure repudiated the Sound
alliance. The office passed in time to Lord Gaara. This file is retained to
ensure no future Kazekage's identity may be usurped unverified. Full operational
detail is held under the classified assassination report.
